{
  "root": "vehicle-create",
  "execution": [
    {
      "skill": "mesh-object-create",
      "content": "# Create Mesh Object\n\nCreate one unit cube mesh object with the requested object and mesh names. Link it only to the requested collection, which must belong to the active scene. Set the exact requested transform and do not rely on selection state."
    },
    {
      "skill": "object-resolve",
      "content": "# Resolve Object\n\nResolve by exact data-block name. Require one existing object linked to the active scene. Reject missing, renamed, or unlinked objects; do not substitute the selected object."
    },
    {
      "skill": "rigid-body-add",
      "content": "# Add Rigid Body\n\nResolve the existing chassis and set `obj.game.physics_type` to `RIGID_BODY`, mass to `800.0`, damping to `0.2`, rotation damping to `0.4`, and friction to `0.8`. Do not use Blender rigid-body world settings."
    },
    {
      "skill": "chassis-create",
      "content": "# Create Chassis\n\nCreate chassis `CapgraphVehicle` in `CapgraphVehicleCollection`. Use mesh `CapgraphVehicleMesh`, location `(0, 0, 1)`, rotation `(0, 0, 0)`, and scale `(2, 1, 0.5)`. Keep one stable object identity while physical properties are added."
    },
    {
      "skill": "keyboard-input",
      "content": "# Define Keyboard Input\n\nUse `W` for forward, `S` for reverse, `A` for left, and `D` for right. Store canonical key identifiers exactly; do not infer locale-specific alternatives."
    },
    {
      "skill": "input-map-create",
      "content": "# Create Input Map\n\nStore the input map as object properties `control_forward`, `control_reverse`, `control_left`, and `control_right`. Set `controls_enabled` to true. Existing unrelated object properties must remain unchanged."
    },
    {
      "skill": "vehicle-controls",
      "content": "# Configure Vehicle Controls\n\nConfigure persistent vehicle control metadata on `CapgraphVehicle`. The final mapping must contain forward, reverse, left, and right actions with the frozen keys and must be enabled."
    },
    {
      "skill": "collision-add",
      "content": "# Add Collision\n\nResolve the chassis, enable collision bounds, use shape `BOX`, set margin `0.04`, disable ghost behavior, and disable compound collision. Preserve rigid-body settings."
    },
    {
      "skill": "collision-mask-configure",
      "content": "# Configure Collision Mask\n\nSet 16 collision bits. Expected group is bit 1 only: `[true, false, false, false, false, false, false, false, false, false, false, false, false, false, false, false]`. Expected mask is bits 1 and 2: `[true, true, false, false, false, false, false, false, false, false, false, false, false, false, false, false]`."
    },
    {
      "skill": "vehicle-collision",
      "content": "# Configure Vehicle Collision\n\nConfigure solid BOX collision on `CapgraphVehicle` with margin `0.04`, no ghost behavior, and no compound collision. Apply the frozen collision group and mask values exactly."
    },
    {
      "skill": "camera-create",
      "content": "# Create Camera\n\nCreate one camera data-block named `CapgraphVehicleCameraData` and object `CapgraphVehicleCamera`. Link it only to the requested collection. Do not replace a camera with the same name."
    },
    {
      "skill": "third-person-camera",
      "content": "# Configure Third-person Camera\n\nUse camera `CapgraphVehicleCamera`. Place it at offset `(0, -8, 4)` from `CapgraphVehicle`, target that exact chassis, link it to `CapgraphVehicleCollection`, and make it the active scene camera."
    },
    {
      "skill": "vehicle-create",
      "content": "# Create Vehicle\n\n## Purpose\nCreate one persistent, keyboard-controllable vehicle in the active UPBGE scene.\n\n## Inputs and output\nUse chassis name `CapgraphVehicle`, camera name `CapgraphVehicleCamera`, active scene, and collection `CapgraphVehicleCollection`. Return the stable chassis identity and final verification result.\n\n## Execution semantics\nUse persistent editor-time UPBGE state. Apply the exact frozen fixture values supplied by applicable capabilities. Preserve valid state when correcting a failure.\n\n## Caveats\nDo not use Blender rigid-body world settings or runtime-only objects. Do not treat selection state or an agent success claim as completion.\n\n## Completion\nComplete only when the actual scene contains the requested controllable vehicle and a full structured verification passes."
    }
  ],
  "verification": [
    {
      "skill": "vehicle-verify",
      "content": "# Verify Vehicle\n\nRun the complete structured vehicle verifier against `CapgraphVehicle`. Success requires exact object, mesh, transform, rigid-body, collision group and mask, input map, camera target, scene, and collection state. Treat any returned failure as incomplete. Runtime failures include capability, property, expected, and actual values."
    }
  ]
}

